        "@value": "The `from` Element is documented by each `to` Element."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "hasDocumentation"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/demonstration",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Demonstrating and monitoring or recording that the item under verification to confirm that a requirement is met by the item under verification."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "demonstration"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "[International Standard Content Code (ISCC)](https://iscc.io/) is a content-derived identifier standardized by [ISO 24138](https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html) for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like `ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI`."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "iscc"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/swhid",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "SoftWare Hash IDentifier, a persistent intrinsic identifier for digital artifacts, such as files, trees (also known as directories or folders), commits, and other objects typically found in version control systems. The format of the identifiers is defined in the [SWHID specification](https://www.swhid.org/swhid-specification/v1.2/) ([ISO/IEC 18670](https://www.iso.org/standard/89985.html)). They typically look like `swh:1:cnt:94a9ed024d3859793618152ea559a168bbcbb5e2`."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "swhid"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/isDeprecatedLicenseId",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Specifies whether a license or additional text identifier has been marked as\ndeprecated."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/authorization",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Authorization specifies the permissions, rights, privileges, or benefits granted to a Role, defining what the role is authorized to access, perform, or receive."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/postalName",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The name of the recipient expressed in text."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/partialAutomation",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Level 2 - Partial automation or task automation. Some sub-functions of the system are fully automated while the system remain under control of an external agent. The system can perform actions for an approved task without requiring the agent's continuous direct control."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "partialAutomation"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ecli",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "[European Case Law Identifier (ECLI)](https://data.europa.eu/data/datasets/european-case-law-identifier-ecli) is a uniform identifier for judicial decisions across Europe. It consists of five mandatory components: the \"ECLI\" prefix, a country code, a court code, the year of the decision, and a unique serial number (e.g., `ECLI:EU:C:2023:94`)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "ecli"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/audit",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An examination typically focusing on compliance with policies, standards, or regulations. Usually this is done during an audit meeting, while the assessment also involves deep and detailed reviews of work products (e.g. requirements, verification specifications, reports etc.)"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "audit"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Hardware/VirtualHardware",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class",
      "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Class that describes an instance of VirtualHardware."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Hardware/Hardware"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#nodeKind": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#IRI"
